<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices - Sept 27.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices - Sept 27.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>International prices for milling and Durum wheat were unchanged to slightly lower as weather forecasts across Canada and the United States improve, the Australian Wheat Board (AWB) said. Wheat indicator prices for multi-grade contracts 96/97 and Durum fell by one dollar.</p>
<p>Prices, FOB, in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		    ASW 10 pct</p>
<p>No 1 DURUM</p>
<p>		    Delivered Port	     Delivered Port</p>
<p>Queensland</p>
<p>    Brisbane	155.75</p>
<p>    Gladstone     n/a</p>
<p>    Mackay	  n/a</p>
<p>New South Wales</p>
<p>    Newcastle     158.75			 198.00</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   159.75</p>
<p>Victoria</p>
<p>    Geelong	 160.00</p>
<p>    Portland	160.75</p>
<p>South Australia</p>
